      "message": "fix(tools): no library exception for a covered shrink body; edit_user_holder writes through HolderShape::component\n\nA user holder with a wider hidden body draws the outline of a library\nshrink chuck, and the component records no source. The library exception\nof HolderShape::of read such a holder back with the library's smaller\nbody. The exception is gone: a covered shrink-fit body never reads back.\n\nThe MCP tool edit_user_holder (merged in #4438) now builds through\nHolderShape::component, as the form does. It refuses NotKept with the\nform's text. Its test fixture moves to a gauge length that shows the body.\n\nFixes #4455\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
