  {
    "sha": "3d9ca49a97bc7aff3132b9aa9e77ce134b254efb",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDNkOWNhNDlhOTdiYzdhZmYzMTMyYjlhYTllNzdjZTEzNGIyNTRlZmI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-28T01:45:57Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-28T01:45:57Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): a gauge length edit never draws the library body over wider steel\n\nThe generic component editor found the built-in holder by name and drew\nits outline at the new gauge length. A user holder with a library name\nand a wider body under the flange envelope then got a body smaller than\nits steel. ComponentGeometry::regauged_holder now accepts the library\noutline only when the holder's outline is the library's at its own gauge\nlength and the new outline is that outline with one cylindrical section\nmade longer or shorter. Each other case is refused by name.\n\nFixes #4496\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f0dd6f072e781b1718a94350e748610f582cc606",
